## V0 Boundary

The v0 machine is deliberately smaller than the proposed cognitive operating
system. It establishes only these operations:

```text
create world
observe Knowledge(value, error, uncertainty, confidence, provenance)
open claim(knowledge, evidence)
challenge claim(falsifier)
acquire/release exact-resource capability
fork child world(parent head, hypothesis)
```

An LLM response is an external observation. Reusing a recorded response is
replay; asking a model again creates a new observation on a new worldline.

The OCaml reducer establishes journal references and exclusive live-resource
ownership. The Sounio adapter establishes the nominal transition shape and
requires every epistemic axis or evidence field named by that transition. One
layer is not evidence for the other.

## Integration Receipt

The executable v0 receipt is
`tools/loom/evidence/loom-epistemic-machine-v0-20260826.txt`. It records the
native Sounio typestate diagnostics, exact-frame named-rule sabotage, OCaml
journal and capability sabotage, Arrow laundering refusal, provider ABI
regression, complete Loom crash-recovery regression, and atomic shared-runtime
install/upgrade/rollback test. The bounded claim above depends on all of them;
none is evidence for the forbidden claims.

## Falsification Conditions

- any `Knowledge` observation is admitted without distinct nonzero value,
  arithmetic-error, uncertainty, confidence, and provenance digests;
- a claim can reference absent knowledge or a challenge can reference an
  absent claim;
- two unreleased capabilities own the same exact resource;
- a capability owner or generation changes during release;
- a child world does not bind the verified parent journal head;
- a mutated or non-contiguous journal contributes an Arrow event;
- removing only the named Sounio axis-binding rule does not admit the exact
  otherwise-refused treatment frame;
- Arrow, a GUI, or an analytical database becomes a recovery authority.
